/vendor/
/composer.lock

# The site's own configuration: a database password and the secret every session is signed
# with. `dpress init` writes it from the template inside the dpress package, and the only copy
# that matters is the one on the machine it belongs to - a committed one is either wrong
# everywhere or a secret in public.
/dpress.ini
/logs/*
!/logs/.gitkeep
/uploads/*
!/uploads/.gitkeep
.idea/
/public/logs/

# Generated image derivatives. A cache: Apache serves one when it exists and MediaController
# makes it when it does not, so a checkout that has none is not missing anything.
/public/uploads/**/*-thumb.*
/public/uploads/**/*-medium.*
/public/uploads/**/*-large.*

# A plugin that is its own repository is cloned into `plugins/` the way a plugin is installed,
# and gets a line here so this site does not commit a copy of somebody else's history. The
# `reading-time` plugin is the exception on purpose: it is the worked example, and it
# lives in this repository so there is one to read without cloning anything.
